<header class="sg-head"><p class="featured-region">Anthem · 1873 · South &amp; Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="sg-title">Jai Jai Garavi Gujarat</h1><p class="sg-local"><bdi lang="gu">જય જય ગરવી ગુજરાત</bdi> / <bdi lang="gu-Latn">Jay Jay Garavi Gujarat</bdi></p><p class="sg-kid" data-say>A poem of 1873 in praise of the land of the Gujarati people. Today it is sung as the state song of Gujarat in India.</p></header>
<dl class="sg-facts"><div><dt>Words</dt><dd>Narmadashankar Dave (Narmad)</dd></div><div><dt>Culture</dt><dd>Gujarati people</dd></div><div><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gujarati</dd></div><div><dt>Place</dt><dd>Gujarat, India</dd></div><div><dt>Date</dt><dd>1873</dd></div><div><dt>Type</dt><dd>Anthem</dd></div><div><dt>The words</dt><dd>Public domain (words by Narmadashankar Dave (Narmad), published 1873)</dd></div></dl>
<div class="sg-body">
<section class="sg-sec" id="story"><h2>The story</h2><p>&quot;<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jai-jai-garavi-gujarat">Jai Jai Garavi Gujarat</a>&quot; is a poem written in 1873 by the Gujarati poet Narmadashankar Dave, known as Narmad, who is considered the first modern Gujarati writer. He wrote it as the foreword to his first Gujarati dictionary, the Narmakosh. In it he gave voice to pride in the region by drawing the bounds of the land where the Gujarati-speaking people lived: Ambaji in the north, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pavagadh">Pavagadh</a> in the east, Kunteshwar Mahadev near Vapi in the south, and Somnath and Dwarka in the west. The region he outlined now forms the modern state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a> in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p><p>The poem is used as a state anthem at ceremonies of the Government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>. In 2011 the government released a recording of it sung by a number of Gujarati singers.</p></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="meaning"><h2>What it says</h2><p>A poem of pride in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>: it salutes the land of the Gujarati people, names the holy places at its four corners, and ends in hope that the dark clouds over Gujarat are lifting and a new dawn is near. Its mood is proud and hopeful.</p></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="words"><h2>The words</h2><div class="sg-show" role="group" aria-label="Show these columns"><button type="button" aria-pressed="true" data-col="orig">Gujarati</button><button type="button" aria-pressed="true" data-col="rom">Romanized</button><button type="button" aria-pressed="true" data-col="en">In English</button></div><div class="sg-blocks"><div class="sg-lyrics sg-cols-3"><div class="sg-colhead" aria-hidden="true"><span class="sg-o">Gujarati</span><span class="sg-r">Romanized</span><span class="sg-e">In English</span></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="gu">જય જય ગરવી ગુજરાત!</span><span class="sg-r" lang="gu-Latn">Jaya jaya garavī gujarāta!</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Victory to proud Gujarat!</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="gu">જય જય ગરવી ગુજરાત,</span><span class="sg-r" lang="gu-Latn">Jaya jaya garavī gujarāta,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Victory to proud Gujarat,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="gu">દીપે અરુણું પરભાત,</span><span class="sg-r" lang="gu-Latn">dīpē aruṇuṁ parabhāta,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Where shines glorious dawn,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="gu">જય જય ગરવી ગુજરાત !</span><span class="sg-r" lang="gu-Latn">jaya jaya garavī gujarāta!</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Victory to proud Gujarat!</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="gu">ધ્વજ પ્રકાશશે ઝળળ કસુંબી,</span><span class="sg-r" lang="gu-Latn">Dhvaja prakāśaśē jhaḷaḷa kasumbī,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Thy scarlet flag marked with love</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="gu">પ્રેમ શૌર્ય અંકિત;</span><span class="sg-r" lang="gu-Latn">prēma śaurya aṅkita;</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>and valour will shine;</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="gu">તું ભણવ ભણવ નિજ સંતજિ સઉને,</span><span class="sg-r" lang="gu-Latn">tuṁ bhaṇava bhaṇava nija santaji sa'unē,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Teach thy children everyday,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="gu">પ્રેમ ભક્તિની રીત</span><span class="sg-r" lang="gu-Latn">prēma bhaktinī rīta</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>the way of love and devotion.</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="gu">ઊંચી તુજ સુંદર જાત,</span><span class="sg-r" lang="gu-Latn">ūn̄cī tuja sundara jāta,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Your kind is high and beautiful,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="gu">જય જય ગરવી ગુજરાત.</span><span class="sg-r" lang="gu-Latn">jaya jaya garavī gujarāta.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Victory to proud Gujarat.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="gu">ઉત્તરમાં અંબા માત,</span><span class="sg-r" lang="gu-Latn">Uttaramāṁ ambā māta,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>In north, Goddess Amba is situated,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="gu">પૂરવમાં કાળી માત,</span><span class="sg-r" lang="gu-Latn">pūravamāṁ kāḷī māta,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>In east, Goddess Kali is situated,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="gu">છે દક્ષિણ દિશમાં કરંત રક્ષા, કુંતેશ્વર મહાદેવ;</span><span class="sg-r" lang="gu-Latn">chē dakṣiṇa diśamāṁ karanta rakṣā, kuntēśvara mahādēva;</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>In south, Kunteshwer Mahadev protects (Gujarat).</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="gu">ને સોમનાથ ને દ્ધારકેશ એ,</span><span class="sg-r" lang="gu-Latn">nē sōmanātha nē d'dhārakēśa ē,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Somnath and the lord of Dwarka</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="gu">પશ્વિમ કેરા દેવછે સહાયમાં સાક્ષાત,</span><span class="sg-r" lang="gu-Latn">paśvima kērā dēvachē sahāyamāṁ sākṣāta,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>are the gods in the west and ready to protect.</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="gu">જય જય ગરવી ગુજરાત.</span><span class="sg-r" lang="gu-Latn">jaya jaya garavī gujarāta.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Victory to proud Gujarat.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="gu">નદી તાપી નર્મદા જોય,</span><span class="sg-r" lang="gu-Latn">Nadī tāpī narmadā jōya,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Have seen rivers Narmada, Tapi,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="gu">મહી ને બીજી પણ જોય.</span><span class="sg-r" lang="gu-Latn">mahī nē bījī paṇa jōya.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Mahi and others.</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="gu">વળી જોય સુભટના જુદ્ધ રમણને,</span><span class="sg-r" lang="gu-Latn">Vaḷī jōya subhaṭanā jud'dha ramaṇanē,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>And seen wars of valiant warriors,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="gu">રત્નાકર સાગર;</span><span class="sg-r" lang="gu-Latn">ratnākara sāgara;</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>and the Arabian Sea with enormous resources.</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="gu">પર્વત ઉપરથી વીર પૂર્વજો,</span><span class="sg-r" lang="gu-Latn">parvata uparathī vīra pūrvajō,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>From the top of the hills,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="gu">દે આશિષ જયકર સંપે સોયે સઉ જાત,</span><span class="sg-r" lang="gu-Latn">dē āśiṣa jayakara sampē sōyē sa'u jāta,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Our gallant ancestors are blessing for victory. Unite all castes.</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="gu">જય જય ગરવી ગુજરાત.</span><span class="sg-r" lang="gu-Latn">jaya jaya garavī gujarāta.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Victory to proud Gujarat.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="gu">તે અણહિલવાડના રંગ,</span><span class="sg-r" lang="gu-Latn">Tē aṇahilavāḍanā raṅga,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>That past glory of ancient capital Anhilwad</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="gu">તે સિદ્ધરાજ જયસિંગ.</span><span class="sg-r" lang="gu-Latn">tē sid'dhrarāja jayasiṅga.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>and king Siddharaj Jaisinh.</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="gu">તે રંગ થકી પણ અધિક સરસ રંગ,</span><span class="sg-r" lang="gu-Latn">Tē raṅga thakī paṇa adhika sarasa raṅga,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Will be surpassed in near future,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="gu">થશે સત્વરે માત!</span><span class="sg-r" lang="gu-Latn">thaśē satvarē māta!</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>O Mother!</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="gu">શુભ શકુન દીસે મધ્યાહ્ન શોભશે,</span><span class="sg-r" lang="gu-Latn">Śubha śakuna dīsē madhyāhna śōbhaśē,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>The night has over and the omen are good,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="gu">વીતી ગઈ છે રાત.</span><span class="sg-r" lang="gu-Latn">vītī ga'ī chē rāta.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>the noon will beseem.</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="gu">જન ઘૂમે નર્મદા સાથ,</span><span class="sg-r" lang="gu-Latn">Jana ghūmē narmadā sātha,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>People dance with Narmada.</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="gu">જય જય ગરવી ગુજરાત.</span><span class="sg-r" lang="gu-Latn">jaya jaya garavī gujarāta.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Victory to proud Gujarat.</span></p></div></div></div><div class="sg-credit"><p>Original: Narmad, as quoted in the Gujarati Wikipedia. Text from <a href="https://gu.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E0%AA%9C%E0%AA%AF_%E0%AA%9C%E0%AA%AF_%E0%AA%97%E0%AA%B0%E0%AA%B5%E0%AB%80_%E0%AA%97%E0%AB%81%E0%AA%9C%E0%AA%B0%E0%AA%BE%E0%AA%A4" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikipedia</a>; public domain.</p><p>Romanized: romanization quoted in the Gujarati Wikipedia (CC BY-SA). Text from <a href="https://gu.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E0%AA%9C%E0%AA%AF_%E0%AA%9C%E0%AA%AF_%E0%AA%97%E0%AA%B0%E0%AA%B5%E0%AB%80_%E0%AA%97%E0%AB%81%E0%AA%9C%E0%AA%B0%E0%AA%BE%E0%AA%A4" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikipedia</a>; public domain.</p><p>English: English translation quoted in the Gujarati Wikipedia (translator not named; CC BY-SA). Text from <a href="https://gu.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E0%AA%9C%E0%AA%AF_%E0%AA%9C%E0%AA%AF_%E0%AA%97%E0%AA%B0%E0%AA%B5%E0%AB%80_%E0%AA%97%E0%AB%81%E0%AA%9C%E0%AA%B0%E0%AA%BE%E0%AA%A4" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikipedia</a>; public domain.</p></div></section>
